            "volume": 0,
            "fadetime": 1
        }
    },
    {
        "text": "They must have leapt out of a fairy tale just a moment ago, stood there imposingly in the garden. They really do exist."
    },
    {
        "text": "Their golden fur gleams scintillant as the sun. The one at the head has pupils of deep brown, and they are now calmly staring at Allerdale."
    },
    {
        "text": "Allerdale, brought by her father, has had several audiences with His Majesty, and seen generations of portraits of the Aslan kings hung on the palace walls."
    },
    {
        "text": "But this is the first time she cannot help the urge to bow her head before such a gaze\u2014for the ones before her seem more awe-inspiring than any monarch."
    },
    {
        "command": "dialog"
    },
